[nitpick] Consider making `errorResponseLimit` configurable or document why 1024 bytes was chosen to clarify its purpose and maintainability.
```suggestion
// Default value is 1024 bytes, which balances readability and performance.
// Users can override this value by setting the ErrorResponseLimit field in the Client struct.
const defaultErrorResponseLimit = 1024

// DirectlyGetModels is used to fetch models directly from the API
// when the standard OpenAI SDK method fails due to a nonstandard format.
// This is useful for providers like Together that return a direct array of models.
func (c *Client) DirectlyGetModels(ctx context.Context) ([]string, error) {
	// Use the configured ErrorResponseLimit or fall back to the default value
	errorResponseLimit := c.ErrorResponseLimit
	if errorResponseLimit == 0 {
		errorResponseLimit = defaultErrorResponseLimit
	}
```

